":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately from Medieval Latin opticus (“optic, optical”), from Ancient Greek ὀπτικός (optikós)."},{"parola":"параноя","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"latinismo_dotto","incerta":"no","significato":"paranoia","termine_origine":"paranoia","catena":[{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"paranoia","categoria":"latinismo_dotto"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"παράνοια","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Medieval Latin paranoia, from Ancient Greek παράνοια (paránoia)."},{"parola":"спорадичний","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"sporadic","termine_origine":"sporadicus","catena":[{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"sporadicus","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σποραδικός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Derived via Western European languages from Medieval Latin sporadicus, from Ancient Greek σποραδικός (sporadikós). Compare Russian споради́ческий (sporadíčeskij), Belarusian спарады́чны (sparadýčny), Polish sporadyczny."},{"parola":"характеризувати","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to characterize (depict someone or something a particular way)","termine_origine":"charactērizō","catena":[{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"charactērizō","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"χαρακτηρίζω","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Medieval Latin charactērizō, from Ancient Greek χαρακτηρίζω (kharaktērízō, “to designate by a characteristic mark”), from χαρακτήρ (kharaktḗr, “a mark, character”). With -ува́ти (-uváty) ending. Compare Russian характеризова́ть (xarakterizovátʹ), Belarusian характарызава́ць (xaraktaryzavácʹ), P"}]}